    "DisplayName": "Lenticular (orographic)",
    "Notes": "The lens that stands still over a mountain. Its signature is what it does NOT have: the base ramp is as long as the top taper, so the section is a symmetric lens rather than a flat-bottomed heap, and the erosion is turned almost off because a smooth surface is the whole point. Anisotropy 0.20 - BELOW one, so the stretch is ACROSS the wind and not along it, and that is what separates a wave cloud from everything else in this library. A lenticular stands in a mountain's lee wave with its crest perpendicular to the flow; the altocumulus next door has the same controls set the other way and is a different kind of cloud for it, not a thicker one.",
